# TypeScript API rules (save as .cursor/rules/typescript-api.mdc)

- `strict: true`. No `any`; use `unknown` + narrowing. Exported functions have explicit return types.
- Validate every external input (HTTP body, query, env, webhook payload) with a schema (zod/valibot) at the boundary; internal code receives typed, validated data.
- Errors: throw typed errors (`class NotFoundError extends AppError`) and map them to HTTP status in ONE error middleware. Never leak stack traces to clients.
- Async: always `await` or explicitly `void` promises; no floating promises. Use `AbortSignal` timeouts for outbound HTTP.
- Config: read env once in `config.ts`, validate, export a frozen object. No `process.env` elsewhere.
- Logging: structured JSON (pino). Include `requestId`. Never log tokens, passwords, full card numbers or emails.
- DB: parameterized queries only. Migrations are forward-only and idempotent.
- Tests: vitest/node:test. Unit-test pure logic; integration-test routes with a real test DB or an in-memory fake — no mocking of the module under test.
- Money: integer minor units (cents) + ISO currency code. Never floats.
- Dates: store UTC ISO-8601; convert to local only at the presentation edge.
